**Finding submitted: TRANSITION — missing (fallback insert).**

**What I checked.** Article XIV (Effect of Termination) in full, Article X (Confidentiality), and targeted searches for "transition", "destroy", "return all copies", and post-termination supply.

**What the document does.** The entire wind-down regime runs one way, in Array's favour:
- 14.2(a)(i) — Ono transitions Clinical Studies and pre-clinical/formulation studies to Array (p0646–p0647), often at Ono's cost;
- 14.2(a)(iii) — Ono assigns Regulatory Filings and hands over all Data and Ono Know-How (p0656, p0659);
- 14.2(a)(iv) — Ono provides customer lists and customer data (p0660);
- 14.2(a)(v)–(viii) — Improvement licences, delivery/destruction of Array materials, trademark and domain assignment, Sublicence assignment (p0661–p0666).

The only mutual text, the first sentence of 14.2(a)(iv), is a Diligent Efforts cooperation covenant confined to transitioning the Product back to Array during the redacted Wind-down Period. It sets no assistance period running from expiry or termination and imposes no Array obligation to return or export Ono's data. Article X has no return-of-Confidential-Information mechanic, so nothing elsewhere cures the gap.

**Cure.** A single insert_after p0667 as a new 14.2(a)(x), carrying only the three fallback elements — application on expiry or termination for any reason, at least 90 days of Array transition assistance, and export/delivery of Ono's Data within 30 days. I deliberately did not import the preferred six-month term, machine-readable format, or certified-deletion tail, and did not disturb any existing subsection.
